# WorkOS live stack — agent-operated, Owner browser-only

App: `C:\w\psiso` · Vite `:3000` · uvicorn `:8000`.

## Owner reality (non-negotiable)

- Owner **never** runs terminal scripts (no Windows Terminal, no `dev.ps1`, no copy-paste PowerShell).
- Owner only uses the **browser** and chat ("pornește aplicația" / live / "oprește").
- **You** start/stop the stack when Owner asks in chat.

## When Owner asks to start (pornește / live / devmode)

1. Prefer **reuse** if `:3000` + `:8000` already healthy — tell Owner the URL; do nothing else.
2. If down, **you** run detached (survives agent session end):
   ```powershell
   cd C:\w\psiso
   .\scripts\dev-detached.ps1
   ```
3. NEVER use foreground `.\scripts\dev.ps1` in an agent shell (`finally` kills FE+BE when the shell ends).
4. NEVER kill ports as part of start. If blocked, report — do not kill.

## Forbidden without explicit Owner GO (oprește / stop / kill / restart)

- NEVER `Stop-Process` / `taskkill` / kill listeners on **3000** or **8000**
- NEVER kill vite / uvicorn / node "to free the port"

## When Owner asks to stop

**You** run `.\scripts\stop-dev.ps1` — do not tell Owner to run it.
